1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,179
After someone dies, the people who loved
them are left with

2
00:00:04,179 --> 00:00:06,269
questions. Where is the will?

3
00:00:06,269 --> 00:00:08,846
Who can act? Which claim comes next?

4
00:00:08,846 --> 00:00:11,284
Grief becomes a paperwork project.

5
00:00:11,284 --> 00:00:15,777
Hearth helps families prepare before that
moment, and gives trusted helpers

6
00:00:15,777 --> 00:00:18,851
and advice firms a clear path through what
follows.

7
00:00:18,851 --> 00:00:23,049
One private workspace, from preparation to
handover to follow-through.

8
00:00:23,049 --> 00:00:26,583
Meet Maria and Elena, a fictional mother
and daughter.

9
00:00:26,583 --> 00:00:29,860
Maria has a will, accounts, care notes and
wishes.

10
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:33,458
Elena needs to know what matters, where it
is, and what

11
00:00:33,458 --> 00:00:34,936
she is allowed to see.

12
00:00:34,936 --> 00:00:39,735
First, prepare. Record trusted people,
locate original documents, and

13
00:00:39,735 --> 00:00:43,163
compare account instructions with current
wishes.

14
00:00:43,163 --> 00:00:47,825
Maria wants both children included, but an
old statement names only

15
00:00:47,825 --> 00:00:50,773
Elena. Hearth keeps that mismatch visible.

16
00:00:50,773 --> 00:00:55,128
With permission, Meta's Muse Spark one
point three reads Maria's sample

17
00:00:55,128 --> 00:00:59,786
policy. The transcription stays
unconfirmed until a person checks it
against

18
00:00:59,786 --> 00:01:00,391
the file.

19
00:01:00,391 --> 00:01:03,582
Muse Wonder one point zero then connects
the records.

20
00:01:03,582 --> 00:01:07,424
It notices that the policy names Elena
while the account summary

21
00:01:07,424 --> 00:01:11,620
says the beneficiary is unknown, and
proposes an insurer confirmation.

22
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:14,354
Each proposal keeps an exact source quote.

23
00:01:14,354 --> 00:01:17,405
A person can reject it or create a task,
with a

24
00:01:17,405 --> 00:01:20,202
responsible person and completion
evidence.

25
00:01:20,202 --> 00:01:22,427
The model suggests. People decide.

26
00:01:22,427 --> 00:01:26,924
Next, handover. Elena's emergency view
shows permitted care information,

27
00:01:26,924 --> 00:01:30,436
while private accounts and personal
letters stay hidden.

28
00:01:30,436 --> 00:01:34,379
An invitation gives access to information,
not legal authority.

29
00:01:34,379 --> 00:01:38,116
After a death, record the report, then
separately review evidence of

30
00:01:38,116 --> 00:01:42,178
death, identity and appointment. The
proper role and evidence are required

31
00:01:42,178 --> 00:01:45,915
for restricted administration. The family
can see which step remains

32
00:01:45,915 --> 00:01:46,565
unresolved.

33
00:01:46,565 --> 00:01:50,852
Now follow through. For an insurance
claim, organise the claimant's

34
00:01:50,852 --> 00:01:55,076
authority, required documents, next action
and preparation packet.

35
00:01:55,076 --> 00:01:59,615
Track submission, insurer approval and
actual receipt separately, so an

36
00:01:59,615 --> 00:02:02,074
unfinished claim cannot look complete.

37
00:02:02,074 --> 00:02:06,538
The estate ledger separates proposed
expenses, confirmed transactions and

38
00:02:06,538 --> 00:02:10,880
reserves. Giving stays optional, with
separate intention, execution and

39
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:15,525
receipt stages. Hearth does not move money
or replace professional judgment.

40
00:02:15,525 --> 00:02:18,627
Meta turns scattered records into
reviewable work.

41
00:02:18,627 --> 00:02:22,336
Deterministic rules protect permissions
and evidence states.

42
00:02:22,336 --> 00:02:26,350
The evaluation page runs those rules and
checks live model output

43
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:29,573
against its source, without claiming legal
accuracy.

44
00:02:29,573 --> 00:02:32,904
The buyer is an advice firm coordinating
families over time.

45
00:02:32,904 --> 00:02:36,889
Our proposed annual service is eighteen
thousand dollars for two hundred

46
00:02:36,889 --> 00:02:40,657
and fifty households. At sixty dollars per
staff hour, three hundred

47
00:02:40,657 --> 00:02:42,841
hours saved would cover the annual fee.

48
00:02:42,841 --> 00:02:45,025
Those savings need customer validation.

49
00:02:45,025 --> 00:02:48,970
Hearth connects preparation, careful
access, claims and follow-through, so

50
00:02:48,970 --> 00:02:52,442
families spend less time searching, and
more time being there for

51
00:02:52,442 --> 00:02:53,073
each other.
